{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":24631,"duration_api_ms":25351,"num_turns":10,"result":"I wrote `src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`, but I haven't run it. My attempt to check for `bpftrace` and the power tracepoints needed approval and didn't run.\n\n- **What it traces:** it prints a line each time a CPU's frequency changes, using the `power:cpu_frequency` tracepoint, with time in ms, CPU number and frequency in MHz.\n- **Idle entries:** it also counts idle entries per CPU from `power:cpu_idle`.\n- **On Ctrl-C:** it prints the last frequency, the number of changes and a frequency histogram for each CPU, plus the idle-entry counts.\n\nRun it with `sudo bpftrace src/49-cpufreq/cpufreq.bt`. It only produces output if the machine's cpufreq driver emits `cpu_frequency` events. On some VMs the driver doesn't, and you'll see nothing.\n\nI didn't add a Makefile or README. I can add a README if you want the example to match the others.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5f94a4fe-1f5c-47b1-aafa-6cd4fe2af80b","total_cost_usd":0.10356805,"usage":{"input_tokens":18,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2759,"cache_read_input_tokens":208256,"output_tokens":2016,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2759},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":26789,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1248,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":351,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000451,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":2016,"cacheReadInputTokens":208256,"cacheCreationInputTokens":2759,"webSearch